  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Seed scoping mission Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is part of the combi-track Sustainable Horticulture in Bangladesh, that focuses among others, on improved access and more sustainable and efficient usage of inputs such as seeds.Currently, some of the main challenges that Bangladesh face in the seed sector, are the limited availability of basic seeds and technical support, risks related to natural disasters and the lack of a regulatory environment for seed export, import and production. Therefore, the purpose of this project is to identify opportunities for seed sector development in Bangladesh and the conditions necessary to start new activities, by means of enabling environment assessments and multi-stakeholder consolidations in both Bangladesh and the Netherlands.The outcomes of this assessment will serve as a strategic input for defining future collaboration and investment in the seed sector between the Netherlands and Bangladesh.</narrative>
  </description>
